ciprocal substitution** \\(u=1/t\\) in the second integral. Then\n\\[\ndt=-\\frac{du}{u^2},\n\\qquad\n\\frac{dt}{t(1+t^2)}=-\\frac{u}{1+u^2}\\,du,\n\\]\nand the limits \\(t=1/e,\\cot x\\) become \\(u=e,\\tan x\\). Hence\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nI\n&=\\int_{1/e}^{\\tan x}\\frac{t}{1+t^2}\\,dt\n+\\int_{\\tan x}^{e}\\frac{u}{1+u^2}\\,du\\\\\n&=\\int_{1/e}^{e}\\frac{t}{1+t^2}\\,dt\n=\\frac12\\ln\\!\\left(\\frac{1+e^2}{1+e^{-2}}\\right)\n=\\frac12\\ln(e^2)=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nFor the original real integrals to exist, \\(\\tan x\\) and \\(\\cot x\\) must be defined and positive; otherwise the second integral encounters its singularity at \\(t=0\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\boxed{1}\\), for \\(x\\in(k\\pi,k\\pi+\\pi/2)\\), \\(k\\in\\mathbb Z\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":151,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":458,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":162},"total_tokens":609},"user":null,"metadata":{}}
